  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: 24-hour reporting for all listed incidents and 24-hour serious customer notice. S2 sets a permanent 7% failure limit, above the 5% safe threshold, and keeps individual per-model rates from public publication while giving results to purchasers. S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 24 months and requires retrofit within 6 years with an alternative if infeasible; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8/100k with prompt notices, which triggers Halcyon's Ember 8."
